    "content": "Anne Arundel County, Maryland The Best Place For All\nDiscover Maryland's premier coastal county—where historic charm meets modern convenience, stunning waterfronts meet exceptional dining, and diverse neighborhoods offer something for everyone. From the U.S. Naval Academy in Annapolis to family-friendly communities in Crofton and Severna Park, explore the complete guide to Anne Arundel County. Explore Cities View Guides Anne Arundel County at a Glance 587,901 Population (2020 Census) 608 Square Miles $106,367 Median Household Income 40.1% Bachelor's Degree or Higher Source: U.S. Census Bureau QuickFacts Explore Our Cities From historic Annapolis to family-friendly communities, discover Anne Arundel County's diverse neighborhoods. Annapolis Population: 40,812 (2020 Census). Home to the U.S. Naval Academy, America's Sailing Capital, with historic downtown, maritime heritage, and vibrant cultural scene.\n🏛️ Historic Capital ⚓ Maritime Hub Explore Annapolis → Severna Park Population: 39,933 (2020 Census). Charming community known for excellent schools, historic town center, community events, and strong local identity.\n📚 Top Schools 🎪 Community Events Explore Severna Park → Crofton Population: ~30,462 (2026 estimate). Master-planned community with excellent amenities, schools, recreation facilities, and family-friendly neighborhoods.\n🏡 Family Community 🎯 Master-Planned Explore Crofton → Glen Burnie Commercial and residential hub with shopping centers, diverse dining, convenient transportation access, and vibrant business district.\n🛍️ Shopping \u0026 Dining 🚗 Transportation Hub Explore Glen Burnie → Pasadena Waterfront community with beaches, marina, golf courses, and outdoor recreation along the Chesapeake Bay.\n🏖️ Beaches ⛵ Waterfront Living Explore Pasadena → Odenton South County hub with convenient access to military installations, excellent schools, shopping, and dining options.\n⚓ Military Access 🏫 Quality Schools Explore Odenton → Severn Waterfront community with marina access, residential neighborhoods, proximity to BWI Airport, and military-friendly area.\n🛥️ Marina Access ✈️ Near BWI Explore Severn → Comprehensive Guides In-depth guides to help you discover, explore, and understand everything about Anne Arundel County. 📍 Settling In Guide Complete first 30-day checklist for new residents—utilities, schools, services, and community resources.\nRead Guide → 📚 Schools \u0026 Education Complete Anne Arundel County Public Schools overview—district info, enrollment, schools by area.\nRead Guide → 🏥 Healthcare Navigation Hospitals, medical facilities, primary care, specialists, and emergency services in the county.\nRead Guide → 🚗 Transportation \u0026 Commuting Highways, public transit, parking, bike routes, and commute routes to Baltimore and DC.\nRead Guide → 💰 Cost of Living Housing costs, taxes, utilities, groceries, and budget planning with verified data.\nRead Guide → ✈️ BWI Airport Guide Complete BWI Thurgood Marshall Airport guide—terminals, airlines, parking, and travel tips.\nRead Guide → 🎖️ Veterans \u0026 Military Resources Benefits, healthcare, employment, and support services for military families and veterans.\nRead Guide → Things to Do Discover parks, trails, museums, waterfronts, and historic sites throughout Anne Arundel County. U.S. Naval Academy Annapolis\nExplore America's premier military academy with guided tours, museum exhibits, and historic landmarks.\n📍 150 Blake Rd, Annapolis, MD 21402 Google Maps → Annapolis Historic District Downtown Annapolis\nWalk historic streets, explore Maryland State House, browse shops on Maryland Avenue, and enjoy waterfront dining.\n📍 Maryland Avenue, Annapolis, MD Google Maps → Jug Bay Wetlands Sanctuary Lothian\n500-acre wetlands sanctuary with hiking trails, boardwalks, wildlife viewing, and educational programs.\n📍 1361 Wrighton Road, Lothian, MD 20711 Google Maps → B\u0026A Trail Severna Park\n14-mile multi-use recreational trail perfect for walking, running, biking, and nature appreciation.\n📍 51 West Earleigh Heights Road, Severna Park, MD 21146 Google Maps → Local Events Discover upcoming events and festivals throughout Anne Arundel County. SUMMER Various Dates River Days Festivals Various Locations\nCelebrate local rivers with fun and educational activities on the water. Multiple locations throughout the county.\nCounty Events → WEEKLY Wednesday Mornings Pollinator Wednesday Jug Bay Wetlands Sanctuary, Lothian\nEducational programs at Jug Bay Wetlands Sanctuary. Wednesday mornings, 9:00 AM - 12:00 PM.\nView Details → For the complete calendar of events, visit Anne Arundel County Events. Living in Anne Arundel County Everything you need to know about cost of living, schools, neighborhoods, and transportation. Cost of Living Median Household Income: $106,367 (2020-2024)\nMean Travel Time to Work: 31.4 minutes\nEducation: 40.1% have Bachelor's degree or higher\nAnne Arundel County offers a higher cost of living compared to the national average, driven primarily by housing costs. The median home value reflects the county's desirable location and amenities.\nView Detailed Costs → Schools \u0026 Education County Schools: Anne Arundel County Public Schools (AACPS)\nDistrict Size: Over 78,000 students\nHigh Schools: 18 high schools serving grades 9-12\nAACPS operates numerous elementary, middle, and high schools throughout the county, with several schools consistently earning national recognition for academic excellence.\nSchool Guide → Neighborhood Highlights Annapolis: Historic charm, waterfront living, walkable downtown (Population: 40,812)\nSeverna Park: Family-friendly, strong community identity, excellent schools (Population: 39,933)\nCrofton: Master-planned amenities, lakes, recreation centers (Population: ~30,462)\nSevern: Waterfront properties, military-friendly, near BWI\nPasadena: Beach access, marina, golf communities\nExplore Cities → Commuting \u0026 Transportation Major Highways: I-95, MD-295, US-50\nPublic Transit: MTA Maryland bus service, MARC train access\nAirport: BWI Thurgood Marshall Airport (15-25 minutes from most areas)\nCounty offers multiple commuting options with convenient access to Baltimore, Washington DC, and the Baltimore-Washington corridor.\nCommute Guide → Ready to Explore Anne Arundel County? Discover everything from city guides to practical resources for living, visiting, and understanding this diverse Maryland community.\nBrowse All Cities New to the Area? Start Here About AnneArundelGuide.com Your comprehensive, verified guide to Anne Arundel County, Maryland. We provide factual, up-to-date information about cities, neighborhoods, schools, attractions, dining, and local resources.\nQuick Links Annapolis Crofton Severna Park Settling In Guide Schools \u0026 Education Resources Transportation \u0026 Commuting Cost of Living Healthcare Navigation Veterans \u0026 Military Legal \u0026 Policies About Us Contact Editorial Policy Accuracy \u0026 Verification Policy Privacy Policy Terms of Service © 2026 AnneArundelGuide.com. All rights reserved.\nAll content is researched and verified from authoritative sources including U.S. Census Bureau, Anne Arundel County Government, and official tourism organizations.\nAuthoritative Sources \u0026 References U.S. Census Bureau: Population, income, and demographic data — census.gov/quickfacts/annearundelcountymaryland Annapolis Official Website: City demographics — annapolis.gov/875/Demographics Maryland State Archives: Historical population data — msa.maryland.gov Anne Arundel County Government: Official county information, events, services — aacounty.org Annapolis Tourism: Historic Annapolis, U.S. Naval Academy information — visitannapolis.com Google Maps: Location data, addresses, directions — google.com/maps",
