    "breadcrumb": "Anne Arundel County, Maryland - Your Complete Local Guide \u003e Anne Arundel County, Maryland - The Best Place For All",
    "content": "Your First 30 Days in Anne Arundel County: Complete Checklist Estimated reading time: 5 minutes\nMoving to Anne Arundel County is a big step, and there’s a lot to keep track of in those first few weeks. This checklist will help you stay organized and make sure nothing falls through the cracks.\nWeek 1: The Essentials Day 1-2: Arrival \u0026 Basic Setup Find the nearest grocery store - Stock up on essentials: food, toiletries, cleaning supplies Locate the nearest pharmacy - CVS, Walgreens, or local pharmacies throughout the county Find the nearest urgent care clinic - Don’t wait until you need it Test all home systems - Turn on water, check electrical outlets, test smoke detectors Locate your trash and recycling pickup schedule - Contact landlord or check county website Set up internet service - Call provider, schedule installation if needed Start utility accounts - Electric (AEP), gas (if needed), water/sewer (if not included in rent) Day 3-5: Official Documentation Update driver’s license address - Visit Maryland MVA with required documents Register your vehicle - Complete registration within 30 days Update car insurance - Notify your provider of new address Set up mail forwarding - Visit USPS office or go online Update your address with employer - For payroll and tax purposes Update address with banks - Credit cards, checking, savings accounts Day 6-7: Healthcare Setup Find a primary care physician - Call your insurance provider for in-network options Transfer medical records - Request from previous doctor if needed Register with a local pharmacy - Set up prescription transfers Find a dental office - Especially important for families with children Locate nearest hospital - Anne Arundel Medical Center or Calvert Memorial Hospital Week 2: Community \u0026 Routine Week 2 Tasks Register to vote - Maryland resident registration available at mva.maryland.gov Join community social media groups - Facebook groups for your specific area Find a local gym or fitness center - County parks have pools and recreation facilities Identify your local library branch - Free internet, computers, programs Register children for school - Contact AACPS enrollment services Find a pediatrician - If you have children, this is important Schedule a family photo - Capture your new beginning in your new home Week 2: Building Connections Introduce yourself to neighbors - Build community relationships Find a place of worship - If applicable to your beliefs Join a recreational program - County recreation has activities for all ages Subscribe to local newsletters - County or neighborhood newsletters Locate emergency services - Know your precinct and fire district Week 3: Deeper Integration Week 3 Tasks Explore your neighborhood - Walk or drive to understand the area Find local parks and recreation areas - Check the county parks map Identify your nearest fire station - Location for emergencies and snow emergencies Set up routine maintenance - HVAC filter change, cleaning service if needed Budget review - Assess your new cost of living situation Update your resume/LinkedIn - Add new address for future opportunities Register for county programs - Parks, recreation, senior services if applicable Week 3: Financial Organization Review all subscriptions - Cancel or transfer services as needed Set up automatic bill payments - For utilities, mortgages, loans Update emergency contacts - Local contacts, local doctor, local emergency services Review insurance coverage - Ensure it matches Maryland requirements Plan your commute - If working, test your commute during actual rush hour Research local tax benefits - Maryland-specific deductions and credits Week 4: Settling In \u0026 Future Planning Week 4 Tasks Complete your vehicle registration - Make sure this is done if not already Schedule annual medical screenings - Doctor checkups, dental cleanings Plan a family outing - Visit a local attraction together Update all social media profiles - New location, new community Research continuing education or professional development - Maryland has opportunities Plan a housewarming or neighborhood gathering - If you want to build community Review and adjust your budget - See how your new lifestyle is working Making It Home Decorate to feel comfortable - Add personal touches to make it feel like home Find your coffee shop or favorite spot - Regular places build community Attend a community event - County often hosts festivals and gatherings Get to know local businesses - Support local economy and build connections Create your local routine - Grocery shopping, gym, weekend activities Important Contacts Summary Emergency \u0026 Essential Services Emergency: 911 Non-Emergency Police: 410-268-4444 (Annapolis), 410-268-4700 (Glen Burnie) Fire Department: 410-266-4300 (Annapolis), 410-268-5100 (Glen Burnie) Poison Control: 1-800-222-1222 Government \u0026 Administrative Maryland MVA: 1-410-863-8000 Anne Arundel County: 1-410-222-3000 AACPS Enrollment: 410-222-8000 Maryland Department of Health: 1-877-404-1112 Utilities AEP Maryland (Electric): 1-800-688-4673 Potomac Edison (Gas): 1-800-477-1004 Anne Arundel Water/Sewer: 410-222-3258 Common First-Month Mistakes to Avoid Not testing your commute during actual rush hour - Test it before finalizing work arrangements Waiting too long to get vehicle registered - Do it within the first two weeks Not setting up a primary care physician - Do this early, appointments can take time Ignoring local traffic patterns - Get to know the roads and parking situations Not joining community groups - Facebook groups, neighborhood associations Forgetting to update insurance - Maryland has specific requirements Not finding local services - Know where the nearest hospital, pharmacy, etc. are Quick Reference: What You Need to Know Vehicle Registration Fees Standard passenger vehicle: $100-150 Motorcycle: $50-80 Additional fees may apply based on vehicle type Maryland Driver’s License Valid for 8 years Requires vision test Must surrender out-of-state license Auto Insurance Requirements 30/60/25 minimum coverage $30,000 bodily injury per person $60,000 bodily injury per accident $25,000 property damage Property Taxes County-wide rate: varies by assessed value Homestead tax credit available for primary residences File with county Department of Tax and License Administration Official Resources \u0026 Government Sources Maryland Motor Vehicle Administration Official Website\nMVA Home: www.mva.maryland.gov Registration: www.mva.maryland.gov/registration Licensing: www.mva.maryland.gov/licensing Anne Arundel County Government Official County Website\nMain County Site: www.aacounty.org County Services: www.aacounty.org/departments Resident Services: www.aacounty.org/residents Maryland Department of Health Official State Health Portal\nMaryland.gov Health: health.maryland.gov Health Care Providers: health.maryland.gov/providers Patient Resources: health.maryland.gov/patients Anne Arundel County Public Schools Official School District Website\nAACPS Home: www.aacps.org Enrollment Information: www.aacps.org/enrollment Family Information: www.aacps.org/families Maryland Department of Transportation Official State DOT Portal\nMaryland.gov DOT: mdot.maryland.gov MVA Division: mdot.maryland.gov/mva Travel Information: mdot.maryland.gov/travel Last updated: May 2026\nUse this checklist as your roadmap through the first month in Anne Arundel County. Tackle items at your own pace, but check them off as you complete them. You’ll be settled in before you know it!",
