    "content": "BWI Airport Guide Baltimore-Washington International Thurgood Marshall Airport sits right in Anne Arundel County, which makes it your local airport. That convenience means you’re usually 10-20 minutes from terminals depending on where you live in the county.\nLocation \u0026 Access Address: 700 Ground Circle, Baltimore, MD 21240\nBWI sits between Annapolis and Glen Burnie, south of MD-3 and east of I-95. The airport owns the land, so while the mailing address says Baltimore, you’re physically in Anne Arundel.\nDriving to BWI From Different Parts of the County From Annapolis: Take MD-3 North to I-95 North, exit at BWI Airport. About 25-35 minutes depending on traffic.\nFrom Glen Burnie: Direct access via MD-295 South. Most drivers know this route well - about 15-20 minutes.\nFrom Severna Park: Take MD-174 West to MD-295 South. Around 20 minutes typically.\nFrom Crofton: Take MD-175 North to MD-295 South. Roughly 25-30 minutes.\nRoutes Most Common: MD-295 (Baltimore-Washington Parkway) is the main artery to the airport. Follow signs for BWI Airport.\nFrom Baltimore: I-95 South to MD-295 South, follow airport signs.\nFrom DC: I-95 South to MD-295 South. About 45-60 minutes depending on DC traffic.\nParking at BWI BWI offers several parking options with different price points:\nRover Lot (Economy):\n$8/day first day, $6/day subsequent days Free shuttle every 10-15 minutes About 10-15 minute drive to terminals Best for trips longer than 3 days Daily Parking (Galleries):\n$15-18/day Covered and uncovered spaces Walking distance to terminals (5-10 minutes) Good for 1-3 day trips Valet Parking:\n$25-30/day Drop off right at curbside Pick up at curbside when returning Most convenient, most expensive Oversized Vehicle Parking:\nSame rates as economy or daily Specific lots for RVs, large vehicles Shuttle service available Airport Website Official BWI website has real-time parking availability: bwia.com\nBWI MARC Train Station The MARC Penn Line runs from BWI Rail Station to Union Station in DC. This is useful if you work in DC and want to avoid driving.\nBWI Rail Station Details Location: BWI Airport Marriott Drive, adjacent to airport\nHours:\nMonday-Friday: 4:30 AM - 11:30 PM Saturday-Sunday: Limited service Parking at Rail Station:\nFree parking available Fill up quickly on weekday mornings Arrive at least 30 minutes before train Train Schedule To Washington Union Station:\nMorning: ~6:00 AM - 9:00 AM (multiple trains) Evening: ~4:00 PM - 7:00 PM (multiple trains) Travel time: About 45-50 minutes Weekend service: Limited, check schedule To Baltimore Union Station:\nMultiple trains throughout day Travel time: About 20-25 minutes More flexible than DC service Ticketing Monthly Pass:\nZone 2 (BWI to DC): Around $150-180/month Zone 1 (BWI to Baltimore): Around $100-120/month Purchase online or at station machines Single Ride:\nDC: $5.75-12.00 depending on time Baltimore: $3.50-6.00 Cash or credit at machines MARC Website Official MARC info and schedules: marylandtransit.com/marc\nRideshare \u0026 Taxis Uber \u0026 Lyft Both services operate at BWI. Designated pickup areas are on the ground floor after baggage claim.\nTypical costs within county:\nAnnapolis: $40-70 Glen Burnie: $25-40 Severna Park: $35-50 Crofton: $40-55 Peak pricing: Expect higher fares during holidays, rush hours, and bad weather.\nTaxis Yellow cab companies serve BWI. Fares are metered.\nBase fare: Around $3-5 plus mileage\nTo Annapolis: $60-90 typical\nTo DC: $120-180 depending on destination\nPublic Transit Options MTA Bus Routes Route 4: Connects Glen Burnie to BWI and continues to DC\nRoute 7: Some service to BWI from Annapolis area\nCost: $2.00 cash, $1.50 with CharmCard\nBWI Express Shuttle services run to various locations. Check current schedules as routes change.\nTerminal Information BWI has one main terminal building with four levels:\nLevel 1: Baggage claim Level 2: Check-in counters Level 3: Departures, security, shops, restaurants Level 4: Airline gates\nThe layout is straightforward. Check your airline for which level to use.\nAirlines at BWI Major carriers include:\nSouthwest (largest presence) American Airlines Delta United JetBlue Frontier Spirit Alaska Airlines Each airline has specific check-in areas. Check your ticket or the BWI website for your airline’s terminal location.\nTips for BWI Travel Weekday mornings: Arrive at least 2 hours early. Airport gets busy with commuters using MARC.\nWeekends: Less busy than weekdays, but still arrive 1.5 hours early.\nHoliday travel: Add extra time. BWI gets crowded during Thanksgiving, Christmas, and summer.\nParking reservations: Some lots allow online reservations, especially during peak travel times.\nMARC tickets: Buy ahead online to avoid line at station.\nRideshare surge: During bad weather or peak times, prices jump. Factor this into your cost calculation.\nContact Information BWI Airport Information: 410-850-6060 Website: www.bwia.com Parking Information: 410-850-7243\nFor more transportation info:\nCommuting Guide Transit Routes Official Transportation Resources Maryland Transit Administration (MTA) Public Transit Information\nMTA Bus Info: marylandtransit.com MARC Train Info: marylandtransit.com/marc MTA Customer Service: 410-768-7000 Anne Arundel County County Transportation\nOfficial County Site: www.aacounty.org Transportation Department: www.aacounty.org/departments/transportation Federal Highway Administration U.S. Department of Transportation\nOfficial DOT Site: transportation.gov Highway Info: fhwa.dot.gov Baltimore-Washington International Airport BWI Airport Official Site\nAirport Website: bwiairport.com Parking Info: bwiairport.com/parking MTA Airport Line: marylandtransit.com/airport Last updated: May 2026\nLast updated: May 2026",
