    "breadcrumb": "Anne Arundel County, Maryland - Your Complete Local Guide \u003e Anne Arundel County, Maryland - The Best Place For All",
    "content": "Veterans \u0026 Military Resources in Anne Arundel County Estimated reading time: 6 minutes\nAnne Arundel County has a significant military presence, with Fort Meade (NSA headquarters), Joint Base Andrews, and Naval Academy nearby. If you’re a veteran or military family, there are plenty of resources available - but you need to know where to look and what’s actually available to you.\nMilitary Installations Nearby Fort Meade Home to the National Security Agency and major military commands. This is the largest military installation in the county.\nWhat it offers:\nBase Exchange (BX) with military discounts Commissaries for grocery shopping Medical facilities for active duty and some retirees Morale, welfare, and recreation programs Child and youth services Access: Some areas require valid military ID for entry. Check base access requirements before visiting.\nJoint Base Andrews Home to the 113th Wing of the DC Air National Guard and other units. Close to DC and offers good access to the national capital area.\nServices:\nAir National Guard programs Family support services Morale and recreation activities Access: Base ID required for most facilities.\nNaval Academy (Annapolis) While not an active military installation in the traditional sense, the Naval Academy has extensive support programs for military families and veterans.\nResources:\nLibrary and educational resources Community events and programs Support services for families VA Benefits Health Care VA Medical Center: The VA Medical Center in Baltimore serves Anne Arundel County residents. It offers primary care, mental health services, and specialty care.\nWhat’s covered:\nPrimary care visits Mental health services Prescription medications (with copays) Specialty care (with referral) Emergency care (with authorization) Enrollment: You need to enroll in VA health care to access benefits. Apply online at VA.gov or visit the Baltimore VA Medical Center.\nTRICARE (for Active Duty and Retirees) TRICARE Prime: Full coverage with a small copay. Requires enrollment and a primary care physician.\nTRICARE Select: PPO-style coverage with higher out-of-pocket costs but more flexibility.\nWhat’s covered:\nRoutine checkups Specialist visits (with referral for Prime) Mental health services Prescription medications Emergency care Local providers: Many healthcare providers in Anne Arundel County accept TRICARE. Check the TRICARE website for a list of local participating providers.\nGI Bill The GI Bill provides education benefits for veterans and their families.\nTypes:\nPost-9/11 GI Bill: Covers tuition, housing, and books for eligible veterans Montgomery GI Bill: Monthly payments for education and training Vocational Rehabilitation: For veterans with service-connected disabilities Anne Arundel Community College (AACC): Located in Odenton, AACC accepts GI Bill benefits and has programs for veterans.\nLocal universities: University of Maryland Eastern Shore, University of Maryland Baltimore County, and others in the region accept GI Bill benefits.\nLocal Support Programs Veterans Service Organizations Veterans of Foreign Wars (VFW): Multiple posts in the county offer support and community for veterans.\nAmerican Legion: Active posts throughout Anne Arundel County provide veteran services and community events.\nDisabled American Veterans (DAV): Offers assistance with VA claims and benefits.\nFisher House Foundation: Provides temporary housing for families of veterans receiving medical treatment.\nCounty Resources Anne Arundel County Veterans Service Office:\nLocation: 1699 West Street, Annapolis Services: Help with VA claims, benefits applications, and local resources Phone: 410-222-3318 Website: aacounty.org/veterans What they help with:\nVA claim applications Benefits eligibility questions Local resource connections Employment assistance Mental Health and Counseling Veterans Crisis Line: Call 988 and press 1, or text 838255. Available 24/7, confidential, and free.\nMaryland VA Counseling: Free counseling services for veterans and their families.\nLocal providers: Many private therapists in the county specialize in military-related mental health issues.\nEmployment and Career Veterans Employment Resource Center: Located in Annapolis, provides job placement assistance and career counseling for veterans.\nJob fairs: The county regularly hosts military and veteran job fairs. Check the county website for upcoming events.\nTraining programs: Various organizations offer job training and certification programs specifically for veterans.\nHousing and Financial Support VA Home Loans What it covers:\nPurchase loans with no down payment Refinance options Construction loans No private mortgage insurance (PMI) required Benefits:\nCompetitive interest rates No down payment required Lower closing costs than conventional loans No PMI means lower monthly payments Local lenders: Several banks and mortgage companies in Anne Arundel County specialize in VA loans.\nFinancial Assistance Programs Emergency Financial Assistance: Available for veterans facing financial hardship. Contact the Veterans Service Office for details.\nTuition Assistance: Some organizations offer scholarships and grants for veterans pursuing education.\nTransportation Military parking: Free parking at many county facilities for military vehicles with valid ID.\nDiscounts: Some businesses offer military discounts on fuel, food, and other services.\nSchools and Family Support Military Family Programs Child Development Centers: Available at Fort Meade and Joint Base Andrews for active duty families.\nYouth programs: After-school programs, sports, and activities for military children.\nRelocation assistance: Programs to help military families moving to or from the area.\nEducation Support School liaison officers: Help military children transition between schools and enroll in AACPS.\nEducational programs: Some organizations offer tutoring and academic support for military children.\nKey Insights Living near Fort Meade and working with military families in the county has shown firsthand how valuable these resources are. But here’s the reality: many veterans don’t know they’re eligible for benefits, and even fewer use them.\nThe biggest mistake veterans make is not asking for help. There are plenty of people in the county who want to support you - Veterans Service Officers, local nonprofits, VA representatives, and community organizations.\nDon’t be proud enough to do everything alone. These resources exist specifically to support you and your family.\nWhat’s Next For more detailed information:\nVA Benefits Guide - Complete VA benefits breakdown TRICARE Navigation - Understanding military healthcare Education Resources - GI Bill and local education options Employment Support - Job resources for veterans The military community in Anne Arundel County is strong and supportive. If you’re a veteran or military family member, you have access to resources that can make your life significantly easier. Use them.\nOfficial Military Resources U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs Official VA Website\nMain VA Site: va.gov Find VA Locations: va.gov/find-locations VA Benefits: benefits.va.gov GI Bill Benefits: benefits.va.gov/gibill Maryland Department of Veterans Affairs State VA Resources\nState VA Office: marylandveterans.org Maryland VA Services: maryland.gov/veterans State VA Contact: 410-974-3810 Defense Manpower Data Center DEERS and ID Cards\nDEERS Registration: dmdc.osd.mil U.S. Department of Defense Official DOD Site\nMain DOD Website: dod.gov Military Installations: dod.mil/locations Tricare Military Health Care\nTricare Official Site: tricare.mil Provider Directory: tricare.mil/findaprovider Tricare For Life: tricare.mil/trl Last updated: May 2026\nLast updated: May 2026",
