    "content": "Tricare Health Insurance for Military Families If you’re military or a military family member living in Anne Arundel County, Tricare provides your health insurance. This guide covers your options near Fort Meade, Naval Academy, and Joint Base Andrews.\nTricare Options Tricare Prime Best For: Active duty service members and families\nFeatures:\nNo monthly premium (for service members) $0-200 per person annual enrollment fee (for families) Choose primary care manager (PCM) Referrals needed for specialists Low copays for care Comprehensive coverage Enrollment:\nAutomatic for active duty Enroll through milConnect website Choose PCM from network providers Can change PCM once per year Tricare Select Best For: Reserve members, National Guard, some retirees\nFeatures:\nNo monthly premium Deductible and coinsurance No referral needed for specialists More flexibility in providers Higher out-of-pocket costs than Prime Enrollment:\nMust enroll online Pay enrollment fee if applicable Choose providers from network Can see any Tricare-authorized provider Tricare for Life Best For: Military retirees age 65+\nFeatures:\nSupplemental to Medicare No additional premium Medicare pays first, Tricare pays second No network restrictions Minimal out-of-pocket costs Eligibility:\nMust have Medicare Part A and B Must be enrolled in Tricare Automatic enrollment for some Tricare Reserve Select Best For: Selected Reserve members\nFeatures:\nMonthly premium Similar to Tricare Select No enrollment fee Coverage when on active duty orders Tricare Young Adult Best For: Adult children ages 23-26\nFeatures:\nMonthly premium Extended coverage beyond age 21 Similar benefits to Tricare Select Anne Arundel County Tricare Providers Network Providers Major Systems with Tricare Networks:\nAnne Arundel Medical Center - Full Tricare network MedStar Health - Participating providers Holy Cross Health - Tricare network Various private practices Finding Providers:\nUse Tricare provider finder online Verify network status before visit Some providers accept Tricare only Call office to confirm Tricare East Regional Office Covers: Maryland, Delaware, DC, and surrounding areas\nPhone: 1-800-645-8299\nWebsite: www.tricare.mil\nServices:\nClaim questions Network provider info Enrollment help Coverage questions Using Tricare in Anne Arundel Routine Care Primary Care:\nChoose PCM from network Annual physical included Preventive care covered Routine labs and tests Specialist Care:\nPrime needs referral from PCM Select doesn’t need referral Authorization may be required for some services Ask about prior authorization Emergency Care 24/7 Coverage:\nGo to nearest emergency room AAMC handles most military emergencies Call Tricare if stable to discuss facility Authorization:\nEmergency services don’t need pre-authorization Follow-up care may need authorization Contact Tricare within timeframe if required Prescriptions Pharmacy Benefits:\nMilitary pharmacy (Tricare Pharmacy) - lowest cost Retail pharmacy network - moderate cost Mail-order available Generic drugs preferred Copays:\nVaries by plan and pharmacy type Generic vs brand name pricing 90-day supply discounts Mental Health Services Covered Services:\nIndividual counseling Family therapy Psychiatric services Substance abuse treatment Access:\nTricare network mental health providers Some require referral Crisis services covered Fort Meade \u0026 Naval Academy Area Military Treatment Facilities Naval Medical Center Portsmouth:\nNear Norfolk, VA Military hospital Some Anne Arundel families use this facility Walter Reed National Military Medical Center:\nBethesda, MD Major military hospital Complex cases referred here Military Health Services Fort Meade Clinic:\nBasic primary care for service members Some specialty services Referrals to civilian network for others Naval Academy Health Services:\nFor midshipmen Basic care available Referrals to civilian network Deployments \u0026 Temporary Duty Coverage During Deployment Active Duty Deployed:\nTricare continues Family maintains coverage Some benefits may change Keep enrollment current Family Member Coverage:\nContinues during deployment No additional premium Access to military treatment facilities Use civilian network if needed Temporary Duty (TDY) Traveling for Duty:\nTricare covers care while TDY Use network providers when possible Keep receipts for claims Some areas may have limited network Claims \u0026 Billing Filing Claims When to File:\nOut-of-network care Emergency care outside coverage area Reimbursement for paid claims Some situations require member filing How to File:\nOnline through milConnect Mail claim forms Some providers file automatically Keep all documentation Billing Questions If Charged Incorrectly:\nContact provider billing office first Then contact Tricare Keep records of all communications Dispute charges in writing Special Programs Tricare Remote For Remote Locations:\nSpecial provisions for isolated areas Different cost-sharing rules Check eligibility if far from facilities Tricare Prime Remote For Active Duty in Remote Areas:\nSpecial Prime options Different enrollment rules Check current policies Tricare Standard Programs Active Duty Family Members:\nCan choose Prime or Select Prime usually recommended for cost Select for more flexibility Costs \u0026 Out-of-Pocket Prime Costs Active Duty Members:\nNo premium Enrollment fee waived Low or no copays Family Members:\nAnnual enrollment fee ($200 individual, $400 family) Copays for visits ($0-30 typically) Out-of-pocket maximum applies Select Costs Deductibles:\nIndividual deductible varies Family deductible higher Reset annually Coinsurance:\nAfter deductible, pay percentage Tricare pays rest Out-of-pocket max protects you Prescription Costs Network Pharmacy:\nGeneric: $5-15 Preferred brand: $15-35 Non-preferred: $35-55 Mail Order:\n90-day supply discounts Same tiers as retail Convenient for maintenance meds Important Contacts Tricare East Phone: 1-800-645-8299\nHours: Monday-Friday 7 AM - 7 PM ET\nWebsite: www.tricare.mil\nmilConnect Website: www.milconnect.mil\nServices:\nEnroll in plans View coverage File claims Update personal info Fort Meade Medical Treatment Facility Phone: 410-803-6000\nWebsite: www.tricare.mil/locations/maryland/fort-meade\nNaval Academy Health Services Phone: 410-293-5462\nTips for Tricare Users Choose PCM carefully - This doctor coordinates your care Know your plan - Understand what’s covered and costs Use network providers - Saves money significantly Get referrals when needed - Prime requires them for specialists Keep documentation - Save all records and receipts Update contact info - Keep Tricare informed of changes Ask about prior authorization - Some services need approval first Use mail order - Often cheaper for maintenance medications Common Questions Can I see any doctor? Prime: Must use network, except emergencies\nSelect: Can see any Tricare-authorized provider\nFor Life: Any provider accepting Medicare\nWhat if I move? Update address immediately - Tricare has regional offices\nNew PCM required - Choose from new area network\nCoverage continues - No gap in coverage\nHow do I change plans? Open enrollment periods - Annual window\nQualifying life events - Marriage, birth, move, etc.\nRequest through milConnect\nFor more military info:\nVeterans \u0026 Military Resources VA Benefits Guide Military Education Official Military Resources U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs Official VA Website\nMain VA Site: va.gov Find VA Locations: va.gov/find-locations VA Benefits: benefits.va.gov GI Bill Benefits: benefits.va.gov/gibill Maryland Department of Veterans Affairs State VA Resources\nState VA Office: marylandveterans.org Maryland VA Services: maryland.gov/veterans State VA Contact: 410-974-3810 Defense Manpower Data Center DEERS and ID Cards\nDEERS Registration: dmdc.osd.mil U.S. Department of Defense Official DOD Site\nMain DOD Website: dod.gov Military Installations: dod.mil/locations Tricare Military Health Care\nTricare Official Site: tricare.mil Provider Directory: tricare.mil/findaprovider Tricare For Life: tricare.mil/trl Last updated: May 2026\nLast updated: May 2026",
